^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-09-28 16:00] observe — 74 live plans, 20+ status spellings, 6 empty untracked plan dirs; no flat entry point; ecology temperature last hand-made 2026-08-24.
 >>[2026-09-28 16:10] decide — Cards open every wip.spw; the card's operator is its lane glyph so lanes are visible before words; phases are a controlled set of eight.
 >>[2026-09-28 16:20] surprise — spw resolve reported 1183 of 1388 plan refs missing: it resolved file-relative only while the LSP falls back to the consumer root.
 >>[2026-09-28 16:25] surprise — Full parse runs ~64 KB/s, lexing ~20x faster; the index generator lexes to locate frames and parses only card slices.
 >>[2026-09-28 16:50] implement — spw resolve tries file-relative then consumer root and reports basis; plan refs missing drop to 32.
 >>[2026-09-28 17:00] implement — index.spw with authored legend and doors; derived phase frames, touches, kin, drift; plan:status and the commit gate read cards.
 >>[2026-09-28 17:05] observe — npm run build already fails on main@3eaab637 (expression-charge.test.ts typing); not introduced by this pass.
 >>[2026-09-28 17:06] implement — Eight agents carded 73 plans from git evidence; every card passes plan-index --check. Field reports folded into the artifact's field_reports and dispositions frames.
 >>[2026-09-28 17:07] surprise — seed latestTimestamp ignored date-only and quoted entry heads (181 entries); refresh would have moved last_stream backwards. Anchored on >>[ heads, tests added, 15 caches refreshed.
 >>[2026-09-28 17:07] implement — spw-marker-audit scans packages/ (119 → 158 markers); CLAUDE.md no longer calls fuzz:boonhonk a groove detector.
 >>[2026-09-28 17:08] taste — kin excludes stranded plans and plans cited by more than a fifth of siblings; what remains reads as prompts, and one matched an overlap an agent had found by hand.
 >>[2026-09-30 16:54] decide — a reader's first move is a fragment that survives a crop. Doors and glance cards name a question. They do not teach the current CLI outline as the longitudinal product.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:26] revise — reconciled commits with git: ~[1] to ~[5] landed on 2026-09-29 (b42f9853, 2c082311, e495d903, 1f17c86e, da5189bb) and moved to done. Added ~[6] (resolve passes path to parse; confirmed resolve.ts line 190 calls parse(source) with no path) and ~[7] (fuzz:stabilize does not run plan-index --check) from the predictable frame. Sharpened the three open questions to name what each unblocks.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:26] observe — the predictable item green_head is answered: 7351fb0a typed the charge test helpers and npm run build exits clean today. The artifact's predictable frame still lists it.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:31] revise — convention: resolved questions and landed commits are kept in ^["done"] (resolved(label) and shipped) rather than deleted; ^["commits"] keeps a pointer comment.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:27] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 5 landed, 2 planned, 0 dropped.
 >>[2026-10-13 12:11] revise — resolve_with_path dropped: since 866826ff a path changes no verdict. The glance trial gets a target, the doors index in the caches tree, which already has the guess-then-check shape. The loose fragment matching in resolve moves to citation-navigation as resolve_anchor_strict.
 >>[2026-10-13 19:49] observe — Spirit, in the Workspace view, tallies annotation kinds as phases: a lens counts as wonder, an intent as action. A census of tracked .spw found 57k particles, 66% in the caches tree and 46% on lines repeated word for word across files (#:layer #!pragmatics in 708), so Potential always dominates and the count is mostly template. The archived vscode-cognitive-surface left seven open questions that no live plan picked up.
 >>[2026-10-13 19:50] decide — The owner moved Spirit's default mapping to operators: the seven phased sigils of SIGIL_SEMANTICS, counted from the AST, with . ground and = binding shown off the cycle. The owner also wondered about pinning expressions. This plan takes spirit as a contour: a masked, weighted view measured against a ground, with a receipt, so it reads alike in every editor and the CLI. See the spirit_contours frame in the artifact.
 >>[2026-10-13 19:50] revise — Added six spirit commits (census in seed, one request for editors and CLI, the view, slices in the workspace, per-concept spirit, pins) and four questions. Routed the archived plan's questions: cross_surface_copy and expert_joy here; capture_decorations to editor-reading-hierarchy; primary_questions and surface_taxonomy are answered by editor-reading-hierarchy's tiers; diff_semantics rides with vscode-editor-contract diff_observation_contract; your_surface_corrections lapses with the archive.
 >>[2026-10-13 20:52] decide — The owner asked how the ecosystem can improve beyond their blind spots as agents grow more capable. Six claims stated without checks surfaced on 2026-10-13 (Spirit's mapping, the atlas drift, orphaned archive questions, the mask label, editor against parser, ghost text), so this plan leans on checking over generating: reader_parity_diff lists where readers disagree, and door_trials gives fresh agents tasks and logs their fallbacks.
 >>[2026-10-13 22:04] note — First reader parity check, on feature/reader-bundle: packages/spw-lsp/src/__tests__/reader.test.ts holds the browser reader's roles to the server's semantic tokens, token for token. reader_parity_diff can grow from it to the parser and the CLI.
 >>[2026-10-19 16:35] revise — User direction and 76e17bd4 prioritize useful scaffolds: trial the new agent route independently of Spirit, keep model comparisons controlled, and preserve failed journeys.
 >>[2026-10-27 10:20] revise — Dispositions in the artifact reconciled with history: archive_ready and stranded were settled by the owner on 2026-10-12 (archive in 90c58bbc, rescopes in each plan stream); spw capabilities, seed-roundness-grades and lsp-custom-request-completions are settled in their own plans. Five stay with the owner: safety-commit-reconciliation disposals, register-phase-evolution, the governance artifact header, vscode-register-explorer, and phase_authority here. Shares added: plan-tooling-design settle_status_from_phase answers ?[phase_authority] and both edit scripts/plans; apposition-cache-granules edits server-index.ts, which spirit_request also touches.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[glance_pattern]: "Which non-plan surface (a skill, a docs spine, a registry) gets the first glance card, so the pattern can be promoted to .spw/patterns/glance-card.spw?"
 ?[phase_authority]: "Retire ~#status, derive it from card.phase, or keep both with distinct meanings? The answer unblocks teaching spw refresh to derive status."
 ?[archive_policy]: "Should #done plans move to _archive automatically once the index lists them, or stay until a human archives them?"
 ?[pin_semantics]: "What does pinning an expression do: set the ground, watch a row across edits, join a named slice, or all three; and is it spelled in the workspace, as =#, or as an editor action?"
 ?[particle_phase]: "With operators as the default, does the Concepts view's Phase grouping become an Aim grouping (#> anchor, #: lens, #! focus), or keep phases as a labelled alternate projection?"
 ?[cross_surface_copy]: "Which words stay stable across strip, atlas, hover, and diff so the editor teaches one language? Carried from the archived vscode-cognitive-surface; phase is the first case, meaning spirit-sequence in the atlas and pipeline in the register explorer."
 ?[expert_joy]: "What exactly should feel joyful to an experienced engineer reading or editing Spw? Carried from the archived vscode-cognitive-surface, where it was left open."
}

^["commits"]{
 .[schema_v2_cards](b42f9853): "&[plans] — schema v2: lane-glyph cards, phases, edges, and an index generator"
 .[resolve_consumer_root](2c082311): "&[cli] — resolve refs against the citing file, then the consumer root"
 .[read_stream_heads](e495d903): "&[seed] — read every stream entry head in latestTimestamp"
 .[scan_package_markers](1f17c86e): "![audit] — scan packages in the marker audit; describe boonhonk truthfully"
 .[card_live_plans](da5189bb): ".[plans] — card every live plan; derive the index; route readers to it"
 ~[stabilize_index_check]: "![plans] — run plan-index --check inside fuzz:stabilize so CI agrees with the commit gate (fuzz:stabilize is types plus runtime tests today)"
 ~[spirit_census_seed]: "^seed[seed] — a portable spirit census: per-frame operator counts from the AST, a row mask, occurrence or distinct weights, a projection from the SIGIL_SEMANTICS phases, lift against a ground, and a receipt of what was masked; a test keeps valence off every phase (needs geometric-analysis-tooling ast_operator_census)"
 ~[spirit_request]: "&[lsp,cli] — spw/spirit and spw spirit serve one census for a ground (workspace, root, file, or frame), so every editor and the CLI print the same numbers"
 ~[spirit_view]: "&[vscode,neovim] — Spirit shows the seven phased operators with lift against its ground, the off-cycle operators beside them, distinct beside occurrence counts, and a resting row; :SpwSpirit prints the same card"
 ~[spirit_slices]: "#[workspace] — .spw/workspace.spw ^[\"spirit\"] declares the ground, count, projection, resting rule (declared particles, and lines repeated in N or more files), and named slices; a reading profile chooses a slice, and every slice prints its receipt"
 ~[concept_spirit]: "&[lsp,vscode] — a concept carries its own spirit, the phase containers its occurrences sit in, on its Concepts row"
 ~[spirit_pins]: "&[lsp,vscode] — a pinned expression (@bc#hash or an anchor) becomes a ground, a watched row whose spirit is kept across edits, or a slice member; needs fragment-pointers and ?[pin_semantics]"
 ~[reader_parity_diff]: "![tooling] — one run reads the corpus with the parser, the LSP token stream, and the CLI, and lists each place two readers disagree with its address; the first row is 0f0bso, one word in the editor and 0 plus f0bso in the parser"
 ~[door_trials]: "![agents] — a fresh agent gets a task, not a question, at each door; wherever it falls back to grep or a throwaway script is logged as a door entry naming the missing tool (fallbacks on 2026-10-13: a regex Spirit census, node parse probes, spw select refusing a scratch path)"
}

